1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
It all began in a tiny village.

2
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:08,080
One day, the ground shook and the floor of the catacombs split.

3
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:11,400
From the fissure emerged a man.

4
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:16,400
He claimed to rule the Golden Country, which vanished 1,000 years ago.

5
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:25,640
The land had prospered, he said, until a mad mage cast a spell that sunk it deep underground, trapping his subjects there.

6
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:30,880
I shall bestow my kingdom to whomever defeats the mage, he cried.

7
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:35,380
Then, the man turned to dust and blew away.

8
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:59,140
Stand fast. This dragon should be no problem for us.

9
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:00,240
Get him!

10
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:04,480
With our skills, we can't lose.

11
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:12,640
Although...

12
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,680
I'm really hungry.

13
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:19,300
Heck, everyone seems a bit sluggish.

14
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:23,520
There was a mistake on our map, so we wasted a day getting here.

15
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:27,060
Then we lost three days of food and a trap we fell into.

16
00:01:27,060 --> 00:01:36,260
After we slay this dragon, we'll have to go back for more supplies.

17
00:01:36,660 --> 00:01:37,020
Brother!

18
00:01:38,460 --> 00:01:39,480
What's with her?

19
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:41,640
Did she get hit with a confusion spell?

20
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:48,440
Huh?

21
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:51,100
No way.

22
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:54,860
We came all this way, just to fail?

23
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:58,820
Get out of here!

24
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:11,620
Leos!

25
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:16,880
Thank goodness.

26
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:19,160
That was close.

27
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:21,900
We'd all be dragon food if it weren't for that spell.

28
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:25,120
Speaking of, have you seen Fallon?

29
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:29,380
She got eaten.

30
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:30,660
What?

31
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:34,000
The spell couldn't reach her in the dragon's stomach.

32
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:35,680
Oh, no!

33
00:02:36,380 --> 00:02:38,040
The dragon's sleeping now.

34
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:39,860
I'll go back for her.

35
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:41,780
Hey, hey, wait a second!

36
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:43,840
We're broke.

37
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:47,620
When we teleported, all of our inventory was left behind.

38
00:02:48,380 --> 00:02:50,100
All except the gear on our backs.

39
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:50,780
What?

40
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:53,120
I've got some more bad news for you.

41
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:53,780
Chilchuk!

42
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:57,140
Two of our party members just decided to quit.

43
00:02:58,240 --> 00:02:58,720
What?

44
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:02,860
They've been getting offers from another party for a while now.

45
00:03:03,380 --> 00:03:04,720
Oh, jeez.

46
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:07,040
Raiding dungeons takes money.

47
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:11,100
The cost of party members, gear, and food can get expensive.

48
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:14,920
Let's say we sold all the gear we have on us.

49
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:22,840
Would that give us enough cash to buy cheaper gear, a little food, some medicine, a few daily essentials, and hire a couple more party members?

50
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:24,180
What do you think?

51
00:03:24,380 --> 00:03:25,000
Not even.

52
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:29,460
By the time we figure this out, my cysts will be digested.

53
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:32,700
You can come back from being chewed to pieces, right?

54
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:35,440
Wasn't someone resurrected after being pooped out?

55
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:37,600
Not that I heard of.

56
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:45,480
Financial problems aside, we need to find something to eat.

57
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:48,380
We almost died today because we were so hungry, after all.

58
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:51,740
Now then, where to eat?

59
00:03:51,740 --> 00:03:54,860
If we want something really cheap, there's the public dining hall.

60
00:03:55,260 --> 00:03:57,760
The Laughing Wolf Tavern has bigger portions, though.

61
00:03:58,140 --> 00:04:00,620
Oh, but that place has a fantastic menu!

62
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:03,740
They make a soup with meat dumplings that's to die for!

63
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:04,360
No.

64
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:07,660
I have to go back to the dungeon.

65
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:09,780
But you need to eat.

66
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:10,960
Here's the plan.

67
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:13,980
I want the two of you to leave the party.

68
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:14,620
What?

69
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,400
I'll take your gear and sell it, and raid the dungeon by myself.

70
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,480
No, that's a horrible plan!

71
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:21,160
You get killed!

72
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:24,660
Listen, this way I won't have to downgrade my armor.

73
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:28,540
And if I'm alone, I can avoid monsters and get back to that floor faster.

74
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:30,360
It's totally doable.

75
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:32,860
Besides, this was all my fault.

76
00:04:33,700 --> 00:04:35,420
I don't want to risk your lives, too.

77
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:40,260
I'm going back there with you.

78
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:42,720
You're not the only one who cares about Fallon.

79
00:04:42,940 --> 00:04:44,860
I would do anything to save her.

80
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:51,260
I'm not going to slow you down, and a powerful magic user like me will come in handy.

81
00:04:51,940 --> 00:04:54,060
My skills are nothing to sneeze at, either.

82
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:57,740
You never know when you'll need a trap disarmed or a door unlocked.

83
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:59,700
You guys are the best.

84
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:07,760
Are you absolutely, positively sure you want to come, even though you face death?

85
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:09,700
Yeah?

86
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:10,380
Yeah?

87
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:14,820
We're going to get all of our food from the dungeon.

88
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:15,600
Huh?

89
00:05:15,980 --> 00:05:18,260
This place is full of monsters, right?

90
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:21,920
So then, the dungeon has to have an ecosystem in it.

91
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:25,520
The carnivorous monsters eat the monsters that are herbivores.

92
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:30,300
And the herbivore monsters eat plants, which need water, light, and dirt to grow.

93
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:35,120
Thus, we humanoids can sustain ourselves in the dungeon, too.

94
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:39,720
So that's it, then.

95
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:41,620
We're really eating monsters?

96
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:43,420
Yep, every meal.

97
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:46,060
Think about all of our adventures up to now.

98
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:49,360
Some of those monsters were tasty-looking, remember?

99
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:51,600
No, they weren't.

100
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:52,800
Are you insane?

101
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:56,160
There are lots of people here who hunt monsters for food.

102
00:05:56,720 --> 00:05:59,460
Sure, and they're all criminals who've been banished down here.

103
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:03,340
They're always sick from food poisoning and blowing chunks from both ends.

104
00:06:03,340 --> 00:06:06,440
Well, you did say you'd do anything to save poor Fallon.

105
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:08,000
I didn't say I'd eat monsters.

106
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:10,100
We don't have money for food.

107
00:06:10,260 --> 00:06:11,060
What else can we do?

108
00:06:11,140 --> 00:06:15,120
Right, but if we eat something weird and get food poisoning, we could all die from that.

109
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:16,220
Huh?

110
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:17,900
Run!

111
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:26,780
Why do they keep letting noobs down here?

112
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:30,800
If they're that scared of walking mushrooms, they should stay out.

113
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:31,200
Oh.

114
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:32,660
Laios, no.

115
00:06:32,980 --> 00:06:33,400
No!

116
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:36,940
I think we just found our lunch.

117
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:38,120
That's gross!

118
00:06:39,180 --> 00:06:39,660
Ew!

119
00:06:39,820 --> 00:06:40,260
No!

120
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:41,400
I don't wanna!

121
00:06:41,980 --> 00:06:44,460
How do you even know the thing's safe for us to eat?

122
00:06:44,820 --> 00:06:46,580
The Dungeon Gourmet Guide says so.

123
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:48,920
It's a basic ingredient, actually.

124
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:52,080
They're supposed to be meaty with a mild flavor.

125
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:53,300
Gourmet Guide?

126
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:55,240
Looks like it's been read a lot.

127
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:58,260
Let's find a more open space and build a fire.

128
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:00,860
I wish we had a few more ingredients, though.

129
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,240
Hear that scuttling?

130
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:05,700
That's a scorpion!

131
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:07,900
I lost my appetite.

132
00:07:08,740 --> 00:07:13,600
Even though we are in a dungeon, this section is always bustling with adventurers and merchants.

133
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:19,060
It used to be the catacombs where the villagers' ancestors were laid to rest.

134
00:07:19,060 --> 00:07:25,480
Six years ago, it was connected to the dungeon proper and has become quite the busy location.

135
00:07:26,660 --> 00:07:29,720
They say monsters come from the bottom of the dungeon.

136
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:35,600
Are they creatures from the surface, transformed by dark magic, or are they from the bowels of hell?

137
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:37,100
No one knows for sure.

138
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:40,720
Either way, they look strange and attack without hesitation.

139
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:43,040
As if they were protecting something.

140
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:50,020
If these monsters can exist deep below the dungeon floor, so too could the Golden Country.

141
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:53,860
You caught it like a crayfish.

142
00:07:54,180 --> 00:07:55,120
That's how it's done.

143
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:57,240
And actually, it's easier than a crayfish.

144
00:07:57,660 --> 00:07:57,940
Hey.

145
00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:00,900
You're a little too into this.

146
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:04,280
Is eating monsters some kind of weird fantasy of yours?

147
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:09,200
Saving my poor sister is the only thing on my mind.

148
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:10,660
Sure it is.

149
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:12,380
All right, I admit it.

150
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:13,840
I do love monsters.

151
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:17,740
I love how they look, how they sound, how they live, and...

152
00:08:17,740 --> 00:08:19,880
I always wondered how they'd taste.

153
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:20,940
He's a psychopath.

154
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:28,940
Do we have to cook this right here?

155
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,360
Everyone's staring at us.

156
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:32,940
But we need the water, and it's just a few steps away.

157
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:35,560
All right.

158
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:36,760
How do we cook it?

159
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:38,660
I was thinking we could boil it.

160
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:41,820
What happened?

161
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:45,640
It's easy to cut vertically, but cutting across is hard.

162
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:50,500
That means diagonal and horizontal slashes will have little effect on walking mushrooms.

163
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:52,740
I learned something new.

164
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:55,460
It looks more like food now that it's sliced.

165
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:56,780
No, it doesn't.

166
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:00,620
Hold on.

167
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:02,580
You're cooking the whole thing?

168
00:09:02,780 --> 00:09:03,920
Aren't they poisonous?

169
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:06,780
The venom from it won't hurt us if we eat it.

170
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:09,480
Are you sure?

171
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:10,060
Yep.

172
00:09:10,220 --> 00:09:12,020
The guide says it's totally safe to eat.

173
00:09:12,020 --> 00:09:12,560
Uh-huh.

174
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:17,640
I knew it.

175
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:18,760
Excuse me, folks.

176
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:18,800
Excuse me, folks.

177
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:21,880
A scorpion hot pot, eh?

178
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:24,180
Can't say I agree with your method.

179
00:09:24,980 --> 00:09:25,880
Who are you?

180
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:28,160
These have to be prepared for cooking.

181
00:09:28,660 --> 00:09:31,700
You have to chop off the pincers, head, legs, and tail.

182
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:32,860
Especially the tail.

183
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:34,900
Gives you to run something fierce.

184
00:09:35,720 --> 00:09:38,140
But the guide said it was safe to eat.

185
00:09:38,380 --> 00:09:40,360
You won't die, but it tastes like ass.

186
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:45,260
Next, you have to slice the sucker up so it heats even and the juices can seep out.

187
00:09:45,540 --> 00:09:47,120
This way, you get all the flavor.

188
00:09:47,780 --> 00:09:49,100
It's easier to eat this way.

189
00:09:49,660 --> 00:09:51,760
Then, you pull out the innards like so.

190
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:53,920
They're bitter and the texture's all wrong.

191
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:57,120
As for the walking mushroom, skin it and lose the butt.

192
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:59,140
Save the feet and throw them in the pot.

193
00:09:59,340 --> 00:10:00,300
They're delish.

194
00:10:00,780 --> 00:10:02,100
The feet taste good, huh?

195
00:10:02,380 --> 00:10:02,640
Yep.

196
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:03,720
Take a whiff.

197
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:04,820
Unique, ain't it?

198
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:07,080
Mushroom foot sniffer.

199
00:10:07,620 --> 00:10:09,460
Your pot's not big enough, though.

200
00:10:09,820 --> 00:10:11,460
So, we'll use mine.

201
00:10:12,220 --> 00:10:13,680
You're weirdly prepared.

202
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:17,360
It'll be bland with just the scorpion and mushroom.

203
00:10:23,540 --> 00:10:24,380
Add this.

204
00:10:24,680 --> 00:10:25,200
Hold on!

205
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:26,460
You can't put those in!

206
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:27,220
Why not?

207
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:28,780
There's no way I'm eating that!

208
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:29,820
You see those?

209
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:30,700
Those are corpses!

210
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:32,980
I'll eat a monster if I have to.

211
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:34,780
But not plants from a graveyard!

212
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:36,080
Tell them!

213
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:38,160
Tell them this tastes great on its own!

214
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:39,860
Who the hell are you, anyway?

215
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:40,240
Up!

216
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:41,320
Up what?

217
00:10:46,460 --> 00:10:48,060
A slime!

218
00:10:48,780 --> 00:10:49,220
Oh, no.

219
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:50,900
It's covering my face.

220
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,680
I can't cast my spells now.

221
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:57,360
The first time I ever died was because a slime got me.

222
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:04,820
Are you okay?

223
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:05,920
Doing great.

224
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:07,780
A little got up my nose, though.

225
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:08,960
Use my hanky.

226
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:11,800
I had no idea you could kill those with a knife.

227
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:14,480
It's easy if you know how its organs are laid out.

228
00:11:15,380 --> 00:11:19,720
Sure, it looks like a globby ooze, but it's actually not that different from a humanoid.

229
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:23,220
This here is how the organs of a slime are arranged.

230
00:11:23,540 --> 00:11:30,000
Compared to a human's anatomy, it's like if you turned your stomach inside out and surrounded your head and organs with digestive fluid.

231
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:33,240
They can sense your breath and like to attack when you exhale.

232
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:38,440
That's why if you shout or pitch a fit like the good lady here, you get slimed.

233
00:11:38,860 --> 00:11:40,120
You can't eat these raw.

234
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:44,420
You first have to wash it with hot water and a splash of citrus juice.

235
00:11:44,860 --> 00:11:49,180
Then you can either pat it dry or rub some salt on it and let it dry in the sun.

236
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:52,180
After that, you got yourself one high-quality ingredient.

237
00:11:52,760 --> 00:11:55,640
If you can, starve one for two weeks, then dry it.

238
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:58,140
I promise that taste is worth the wait.

239
00:11:58,140 --> 00:12:01,740
By the way, this is a portable slime dryer I made myself.

240
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:06,580
Just lock it in there like so, and it'll dry out nicely as you're walking around.

241
00:12:07,160 --> 00:12:09,040
It'll be a while before that one's good.

242
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:11,760
But this one's ready to go.

243
00:12:11,900 --> 00:12:12,080
Oh.

244
00:12:12,620 --> 00:12:13,740
We'll add it to your pot.

245
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:16,280
Thanks, but can you spare it?

246
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:17,120
Sure.

247
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:22,540
You don't know how happy I am to have found someone else who's as into monster food as I am.

248
00:12:23,140 --> 00:12:27,440
I've been studying the monsters in here and how to cook them up for over ten years now.

249
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:28,380
Ten years?

250
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:30,860
Has this dungeon been around for that long?

251
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:33,360
I'll have this ready in a bit.

252
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:53,060
It's ready.

253
00:12:57,440 --> 00:13:01,320
So, huge scorpions turn red when boiled.

254
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:03,900
This turned out better than the recipe looked in the guide.

255
00:13:04,940 --> 00:13:07,040
This shouldn't smell as good as it does.

256
00:13:07,520 --> 00:13:10,240
Cook it long enough and the heat shrinks the meat in the shell.

257
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:11,700
Makes it easier to pull out.

258
00:13:12,580 --> 00:13:13,400
You're right.

259
00:13:16,860 --> 00:13:17,700
It's good!

260
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:19,620
I know, isn't it?

261
00:13:19,620 --> 00:13:22,360
The preparation totally changed the flavor.

262
00:13:22,660 --> 00:13:24,220
I know, didn't it?

263
00:13:24,580 --> 00:13:26,280
It tastes so good!

264
00:13:26,620 --> 00:13:28,240
I know, doesn't it?

265
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:33,180
Alright, let me try it!

266
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:36,320
What are these?

267
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:38,240
Dried slime innards.

268
00:13:39,340 --> 00:13:42,920
So good!

269
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:46,140
I never thought a slime could taste like this.

270
00:13:46,580 --> 00:13:48,820
They're amazing, soaked in fruit juice, too.

271
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:52,180
Mmm, those yummy roots you put in are nice and fluffy.

272
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:54,020
Technically, those aren't roots.

273
00:13:54,380 --> 00:13:57,440
They're the stems of a plant that grows upside down in the dungeon.

274
00:13:57,880 --> 00:13:59,980
This algae is soft and delicious, too.

275
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:02,280
Is this something that also grows here?

276
00:14:02,880 --> 00:14:04,380
Nah, that's just plain old algae.

277
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:05,860
You find it wherever it's dank.

278
00:14:05,860 --> 00:14:10,500
All this time, and I never knew this dungeon had so much yummy stuff in it.

279
00:14:14,660 --> 00:14:16,560
Ugh, I'm stuffed.

280
00:14:16,920 --> 00:14:18,880
Perhaps now's a good time for introductions.

281
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:20,840
Yes, of course.

282
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:22,160
My name's Senshi.

283
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:23,960
It means seeker in dwarvish.

284
00:14:24,560 --> 00:14:25,540
My name's Laios.

285
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:27,240
That's Marcil the Mage.

286
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:28,700
And Chilchuk the Piclock.

287
00:14:29,060 --> 00:14:31,720
Something tells me you three are on a mission.

288
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:33,080
Oh, well.

289
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:37,600
On one of the lower levels, a member of our party got eaten by a monster.

290
00:14:38,340 --> 00:14:40,500
We have to save her before she's digested.

291
00:14:41,040 --> 00:14:42,560
I'm sorry, that's horrible.

292
00:14:43,020 --> 00:14:43,740
Which monster?

293
00:14:44,160 --> 00:14:46,140
A dragon with crimson scales.

294
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,380
Crimson scales on a lower level?

295
00:14:49,700 --> 00:14:50,780
That's a red dragon!

296
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:55,500
I hear dragons mostly sleep because they're so big and need to conserve their energy.

297
00:14:56,180 --> 00:14:58,760
Their digestion should be slower than other monsters.

298
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:01,040
I sure hope that's true.

299
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:02,060
Please.

300
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:05,260
Would you allow me to join your party?

301
00:15:05,740 --> 00:15:07,140
Sure, if you'd like to.

302
00:15:07,980 --> 00:15:09,900
Actually, it'd be a great help to us.

303
00:15:10,580 --> 00:15:11,220
I would?

304
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:12,760
Fantastic.

305
00:15:13,140 --> 00:15:14,180
Thanks so much.

306
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:15,280
No, thank you.

307
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:19,340
For years now, I dreamed of cooking one of those red dragons.

308
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:22,340
I have so many recipes in mind.

309
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:25,540
Steaks or hamburgers are classic and easy enough.

310
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:28,220
Ooh, Shabu Shabu would be amazing, too.

311
00:15:28,220 --> 00:15:31,260
Or yakudon, as long as we have enough eggs.

312
00:15:31,260 --> 00:15:37,220
Is it right to eat what ate one of us?

313
00:15:37,220 --> 00:15:42,580
The thought crossed everyone's minds then, but no one said anything.

314
00:15:42,580 --> 00:15:47,480
The second floor.

315
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:54,440
Here, strange vistas stretched before them, unlike the village's musty catacombs on the first floor.

316
00:15:54,440 --> 00:16:00,680
Scholars say this is the tallest tower of the Golden Castle, stretching up from deep below.

317
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:06,280
These trees are so tall, and I always wondered, how come they don't poke through to the surface?

318
00:16:07,220 --> 00:16:09,520
Maybe the curse on this place won't let them.

319
00:16:11,380 --> 00:16:13,060
You okay there, Marcel?

320
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:16,040
Yeah, my foot got stuck on a plank.

321
00:16:16,300 --> 00:16:17,720
We've been walking a while now.

322
00:16:18,340 --> 00:16:19,040
We should rest.

323
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:22,200
Let's find a place to set up camp and get some sleep.

324
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:27,480
Hey, do you remember that time we spent the night here in one of the hollowed-out trees?

325
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:28,860
Yeah, I do.

326
00:16:29,160 --> 00:16:31,640
I made pork soup and got burned so bad.

327
00:16:33,020 --> 00:16:33,500
Soup.

328
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:35,060
Are you hungry?

329
00:16:35,740 --> 00:16:39,160
I got some of that scorpion broth from lunch, if you want.

330
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:40,140
No thanks.

331
00:16:40,560 --> 00:16:41,420
Oh, I know.

332
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,860
We should hunt us a monster for our dinner.

333
00:16:44,300 --> 00:16:44,820
Ah.

334
00:16:46,420 --> 00:16:48,160
What would you like to eat instead, then?

335
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:48,820
Huh?

336
00:16:49,500 --> 00:16:51,660
If you're craving something, I'll try making that.

337
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:54,280
That's nice of you to offer, but...

338
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:57,960
It's gonna have monster in it, right?

339
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:02,640
As long as it's edible, I'm fine with whatever.

340
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:05,820
What kind of monsters appear around here again?

341
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:08,080
Well, hmm.

342
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:10,540
Big bats and giant rats.

343
00:17:10,740 --> 00:17:12,640
I'm not eating unhygienic things!

344
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:13,760
Forest goblins.

345
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,340
Same with demi-humans.

346
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:16,360
Living armor?

347
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:17,580
Metal.

348
00:17:17,580 --> 00:17:19,200
That's it?

349
00:17:19,360 --> 00:17:20,440
There's nothing normal?

350
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:22,340
Aren't there birds or fruit?

351
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:23,680
Oh, my God.

352
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:26,960
First you say I'm fine with anything, then hate whatever we suggest.

353
00:17:27,080 --> 00:17:27,960
You're that type.

354
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:28,380
What?

355
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:30,240
I just don't want to eat gross things!

356
00:17:30,620 --> 00:17:33,100
There are normal animals here, but they're docile.

357
00:17:33,100 --> 00:17:35,120
Well, we'd have to set traps and wait.

358
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:38,400
A duck isn't gonna walk by carrying a green onion.

359
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:39,560
I know.

360
00:17:39,780 --> 00:17:40,820
You have a point.

361
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:45,480
But this is a dungeon, so it might have dire ducks with man-eating green onions.

362
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:47,520
Now there's something fun and tasty.

363
00:17:47,520 --> 00:17:50,320
I don't share your optimism for it.

364
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:54,300
Well, this time of year, there's plenty of nuts and fruits around.

365
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:55,480
What?

366
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:56,260
There are?

367
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:57,720
Mm-hmm.

368
00:17:57,720 --> 00:18:02,200
Ah-ha!

369
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:03,700
A man-eating fruit plant!

370
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:04,640
I should have known!

371
00:18:04,800 --> 00:18:08,140
Actually, man-eating is just a general term for it.

372
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:09,840
See that flower?

373
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:14,160
Its formal name is Barisalia, and it grows along trails animals use.

374
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:19,240
It produces fluid strands, like spider silk, and when a creature touches it,

375
00:18:19,380 --> 00:18:24,340
it can't digest anything, so it doesn't eat the things it catches.

376
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:26,020
It uses them for fertilizer.

377
00:18:26,540 --> 00:18:29,620
It can use a human for fertilizer, too, then.

378
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:32,100
You know the vegetables you have no problem eating?

379
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:35,780
Those grow in soil, fertilized by animal corpses and poop.

380
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:38,800
Right, but I don't have a problem eating those.

381
00:18:39,040 --> 00:18:40,100
Don't freak out.

382
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:41,560
We're on the second floor.

383
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:45,380
A corpse retriever would have come and picked up any dead bodies by now.

384
00:18:45,620 --> 00:18:47,660
They check these plants all the time.

385
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:52,000
This ain't the lower floors, so there's no way someone was left here for fertilizer.

386
00:18:52,740 --> 00:18:53,920
I don't know.

387
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:56,920
Sneaking up to pick one will be tough.

388
00:18:57,520 --> 00:18:59,200
All right, then we fight it.

389
00:19:01,300 --> 00:19:02,280
Step aside!

390
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:05,680
I can destroy them all with one spell.

391
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:09,440
Spellai, Jeptum, Bufelms.

392
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:15,900
Stop that, you idiot!

393
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:16,740
What?

394
00:19:16,980 --> 00:19:17,120
Why?

395
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:24,400
You want to destroy all the fruit, too?

396
00:19:24,840 --> 00:19:26,520
There's an ironclad rule here.

397
00:19:26,860 --> 00:19:28,120
Take only what you can eat.

398
00:19:28,580 --> 00:19:29,900
Stop lecturing and help!

399
00:19:29,900 --> 00:19:32,700
No, no, no, no, no!

400
00:19:32,780 --> 00:19:33,160
Let go!

401
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:40,660
It can't digest anything, huh?

402
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:42,500
It's totally digesting him!

403
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:42,880
What?

404
00:19:43,380 --> 00:19:45,400
Oh, well, some have digestive tracts.

405
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:47,040
It depends on the species.

406
00:19:47,580 --> 00:19:50,140
By the way, the species that has you is parasitic.

407
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:51,940
It plants its seeds under your skin.

408
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:53,660
You're not helping!

409
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:56,560
Stay as still as you can.

410
00:19:57,460 --> 00:19:59,700
These plant-type monsters have lots of limbs.

411
00:20:00,260 --> 00:20:02,720
If I took them on one at a time, we'd be here all day.

412
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:05,440
I only have to attack one spot.

413
00:20:06,140 --> 00:20:06,900
It's root!

414
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:14,180
Are you okay?

415
00:20:14,180 --> 00:20:16,680
Uh, yeah, nothing's broken.

416
00:20:17,520 --> 00:20:18,300
How was it?

417
00:20:18,660 --> 00:20:18,960
Huh?

418
00:20:19,580 --> 00:20:23,120
Like I told you before, this species leaves its seeds under your skin.

419
00:20:23,420 --> 00:20:24,680
It's called a shadow tail.

420
00:20:25,240 --> 00:20:28,820
Unlike the barisalia type that squeezes you till your bones break,

421
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:32,160
this type needs to keep whatever it traps with its vines alive.

422
00:20:32,560 --> 00:20:35,620
It squeezes its prey just enough so it can't escape,

423
00:20:35,860 --> 00:20:38,060
but it's still relatively comfortable in its clutches,

424
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:40,620
which could feel kind of cozy.

425
00:20:41,120 --> 00:20:41,680
Did it?

426
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:45,520
I upset her again.

427
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:48,540
Yeah, you got intensely weird at the end there.

428
00:21:00,020 --> 00:21:01,440
First, a light steaming.

429
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:04,880
Then you cut around the stem like so.

430
00:21:05,380 --> 00:21:06,360
Give a little twist.

431
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:09,220
Then pull, and the seeds will come right out.

432
00:21:09,220 --> 00:21:14,420
Next, you peel the skin off and pound it till it's nice and soft.

433
00:21:14,620 --> 00:21:16,740
Then line the bottom of the pan with it.

434
00:21:17,360 --> 00:21:19,420
Give the unripe fruit a good mashing,

435
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:22,180
add a dash of slime and a bit of scorpion broth,

436
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:24,040
and mix till it's good and thick.

437
00:21:24,660 --> 00:21:26,240
Once it's got a smooth consistency,

438
00:21:26,700 --> 00:21:28,700
pour in the rest of the scorpion broth

439
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:30,300
and a handful of the chopped fruit,

440
00:21:30,540 --> 00:21:31,560
mix it up a little bit,

441
00:21:31,700 --> 00:21:33,380
then pour it into the frying pan.

442
00:21:33,720 --> 00:21:35,140
Let it cook a bit.

443
00:21:35,140 --> 00:21:37,500
I just want to see if I can grow this on the surface.

444
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:39,260
That's a stupid idea.

445
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:39,840
No!

446
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:43,900
And when you see it start bubbling like that,

447
00:21:44,160 --> 00:21:45,580
drop in the rest of the fruit.

448
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:47,840
Perfect.

449
00:21:49,040 --> 00:21:49,820
It's ready.

450
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:53,240
It's a tart.

451
00:21:53,740 --> 00:21:55,100
Looks like it, but it's not.

452
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:56,940
The crust keeps it from burning.

453
00:21:57,220 --> 00:21:58,040
Don't eat that part.

454
00:21:59,260 --> 00:22:00,380
It's real salty.

455
00:22:00,700 --> 00:22:02,060
I thought it'd taste more sweet.

456
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:02,640
Yeah.

457
00:22:02,900 --> 00:22:03,780
It's good, though.

458
00:22:04,460 --> 00:22:05,900
Go on, try it.

459
00:22:06,080 --> 00:22:07,540
I'm pretty sure you'll like the flavor.

460
00:22:08,460 --> 00:22:10,180
You didn't make this with the plant

461
00:22:10,180 --> 00:22:11,860
the corpse fell out of, did you?

462
00:22:12,180 --> 00:22:13,280
No, just its fruit.

463
00:22:13,700 --> 00:22:15,660
The gelatin from the stem of that species

464
00:22:15,660 --> 00:22:16,960
would have made this dish come out

465
00:22:16,960 --> 00:22:18,260
a whole lot better, though.

466
00:22:18,660 --> 00:22:20,580
It's just not firm enough with the slime.

467
00:22:23,100 --> 00:22:23,500
Ow.

468
00:22:23,500 --> 00:22:29,200
Wow, this is really good.

469
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:31,900
The fertilizer-type fruit is juicy and sweet,

470
00:22:31,980 --> 00:22:33,860
while the digesting-type fruit is savory.

471
00:22:34,460 --> 00:22:36,400
I bet the animals love these, too.

472
00:22:36,620 --> 00:22:38,520
Must be hard for the plant to make enough fruit

473
00:22:38,520 --> 00:22:39,580
to keep up with demand.

474
00:22:40,140 --> 00:22:41,560
What's the point making it,

475
00:22:41,640 --> 00:22:42,920
if it's just going to get eaten?

476
00:22:43,280 --> 00:22:45,080
Well, it is a carnivorous plant.

477
00:22:45,400 --> 00:22:48,200
It makes fruit to attract the animals it eats to survive.

478
00:22:48,520 --> 00:22:49,780
That makes sense.

479
00:22:50,140 --> 00:22:53,420
Then being delicious is part of the plant's strategy.

480
00:22:53,920 --> 00:22:54,760
How clever.

481
00:22:56,760 --> 00:22:59,920
Now you see the appeal of monsters.

482
00:23:00,300 --> 00:23:01,040
Aren't they great?

483
00:23:01,200 --> 00:23:02,100
As if!

484
00:23:02,100 --> 00:23:11,960
Well, what do we do about him?

485
00:23:12,240 --> 00:23:14,280
We'd lose time dragging him back to town.

486
00:23:15,100 --> 00:23:17,240
Maybe I can resurrect him with my magic.

487
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:18,780
Don't risk it.

488
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:20,500
The spell could backfire.

489
00:23:21,160 --> 00:23:23,240
If we just leave him where people can see him,

490
00:23:23,300 --> 00:23:24,440
he'll get picked up eventually.

491
00:23:24,800 --> 00:23:25,820
That's a great idea.

492
00:23:25,820 --> 00:23:29,320
This works, I think.

493
00:23:30,580 --> 00:23:33,140
Kind of reminds you of the Galos, doesn't it?

494
00:23:33,140 --> 00:23:39,300
That night, Marcelle had a nightmare.

495
00:23:41,100 --> 00:23:42,220
Dungeon food.

496
00:23:42,660 --> 00:23:44,260
Eat or be eaten.

497
00:23:45,220 --> 00:23:47,300
There is no hierarchy to it,

498
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:49,080
just the reality that to eat

499
00:23:49,080 --> 00:23:50,440
is the privilege of the living.

500
00:23:50,440 --> 00:23:52,840
Ah, dungeon food.

501
00:23:53,520 --> 00:23:55,180
Delicious in dungeon.

502
00:23:55,180 --> 00:23:56,080
cool.

503
00:23:56,080 --> 00:23:56,360
Have a good one.

504
00:23:56,780 --> 00:23:57,220
See you next, 1989.

505
00:23:57,720 --> 00:23:58,080
98% of leaves.

506
00:23:58,340 --> 00:24:00,700
Rocks, Woods and

507
00:24:01,960 --> 00:24:03,000
Rocks, Unsuriegen.

508
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:17,420
Alright.

509
00:24:17,600 --> 00:24:18,000
Here is my opinion.

510
00:24:18,100 --> 00:24:18,640
I got more.

511
00:24:19,420 --> 00:24:19,540
See you next,

512
00:24:19,700 --> 00:24:20,280
염.

